# SECURE ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION TEMPLATE
# DO NOT COMMIT THIS FILE - USE ONLY AS TEMPLATE
# 
# To configure environment variables for production:
# 1. Create .env file with secure values
# 2. Use wrangler secret put for Cloudflare secrets
# 3. Never commit actual secrets to version control
#
# Example commands:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))" > .env.secrets
#   echo "JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=$(node -e \"console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))\")" >> .env
#
# SECURITY REMINDERS:
# - JWT_ACCESS_SECRET: 32+ characters, strong random value
# - XENDIT_CALLBACK_TOKEN: unique per environment
# - Never hardcode secrets in source code
# - Use wrangler secret put for Cloudflare secrets
# - Validate with env.validation.ts before deployment